#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""precheck: catch Open Kernel Challenge failures locally, before spending an `okc check`.

    tools/precheck <submission.py> [--problem NAME] [--lint-only] [--no-trace] [--json]

Stage 1 (lint) is pure Python on the host. Stages 2-4 run inside the okc-precheck Docker
image (tools/Dockerfile: CUDA 13.0.3, torch 2.14.1+cu130, triton 3.8.0, arm64, no GPU):
  2. build: every load_inline / cpp_extension.load the file makes, with its own flags, for
     the judge's arch defaults, plus ptxas -v resource usage per kernel;
  3. trace: prepare() and kernel_fn() run on an emulated H200 (meta tensors, stubbed CUDA
     runtime and stubbed sglang/flashinfer/...) over the scored shapes, the judge's test
     shapes and nearby shapes, recording host syncs, exceptions and launches (verdicts: trace_status);
  4. triton: every @triton.jit specialization the trace launched, compiled for sm_90a,
     with registers, spills and shared memory.
See the Tools section of README.md for what each stage catches and what it cannot.
Import checks use an optional source tree supplied with --scout or OKC_SCOUT; without it, import inspection is explicitly skipped.
"""
